It is quiet in the café now.
The customers are few.
Sunita is with me near the counter.
She teaches me a new task.
"Maya, look here," Sunita says.
She cuts the soft bun quickly.
She applies a lot of butter inside.
I take the second bun too.
I cut it with a knife.
Then I apply butter there properly.
Sunita smiles and says, "Very good, Maya."
This task is rhythmic.
I do this work with joy.
Today I am learning to do many tasks.
First coffee, and now bun maska.
It is only one morning.
But I learned a lot.
